Description: Local GPU-accelerated and multi-model audio separation
 melband-roformer is a CLI (and optional GTK4 GUI) for local vocal/instrumental
 separation using Mel-Band RoFormer, with NVIDIA CUDA acceleration when
 available and automatic CPU fallback. The separate mseparate command analyzes
 music and can execute verified multi-model separation plans, including the
 six-stem HT-Demucs ONNX backend. When explicitly enabled, input WAVs can be
 converted to a model's required sample rate in temporary files; output stems
 retain the model's output sample rate. No audio is sent to a network service.
 .
 This package wraps the upstream melband-roformer-infer Python project
 (MIT licensed) and ships a self-contained Python environment (including
 PyTorch) under /usr/lib/melband-roformer/venv so it cannot conflict with
 the system Python or other Python applications. Model weights (~913 MB)
 are NOT included in this package; they are downloaded on first use with
 explicit user confirmation and sha256 verification. Requires a
 user-installed NVIDIA driver for GPU use (this package does not install
 or manage any NVIDIA kernel driver or CUDA toolkit).
 .
 Run `melband-roformer --info` or `melband-roformer --self-test` after
 installing to check your environment. Run `mseparate --help` for the
 independent analysis command.
